ok - fm-test-queue.sh: warm delta prepared in 16s; mismatch falls back and uncertain execution does not
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: rsync paths, delta shallow, stale lock, nested staging, and quick-check self-heal hold
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: help prints the header and malformed calls are usage errors
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: high load offloads current source and preserves arguments and failure status
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: unreachable hosts preserve local admission; threshold is configurable
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: offload is per-project opt-in; a failed upload runs locally
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: run returns the command's status, keeps its stdio, and leaves
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: runs are served one at a time in ticket order
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: no more runs are served at once than there are slots
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: the reserved slot serves the oldest at any load and the second slot obeys the ceiling
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: a signal releases the ticket and the slot
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: surviving workload children keep slots and abandoned tickets are reclaimed
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: nonleader grandchildren follow the documented lifetime limit
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: a leaked background child in the wrapper's own group is reaped and frees the slot
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: the next run wakes a dead wrapper's stopped holder, which reaps its straggler, and takes the slot
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: a killed wrapper's holder reaps its straggler with no later run
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: a holder outlasting its wrapper waits for a child still recording itself
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: a wrapper killed mid-reap leaves its holder to finish the reap
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: a zombie wrapper whose caller still reads its output does not stall its holder
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: a process substitution started before an exec into the queue keeps its output
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: a snapshot failure during the exit reap leaves the holder to retry
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: a dead holder's nap is reaped, not spared as a caller stage
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: an unread holder start time neither hangs the run nor holds the slot
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: a matching group id without a live holder in it is never reaped
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: a pipeline stage that outlives its caller is not reaped
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: a remote straggler is reaped and cannot hold the SSH output open
ok - fm-watchdog.test.sh: no fixture outlives its suite, even one killed outright or under the queue
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: child liveness requires the recorded start time
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: a lock left by a dead process is broken
ok - fm-test-queue.sh: a delayed reclaimer cannot remove a replacement live lock
